      "content": "That rhythmic thumping is likely caused by sediment buildup at the bottom of the tank which prevents water from heating evenly. Before calling a plumber, you can safely turn off the power or gas supply and try to drain a small amount of water into the standpipe to see if the noise stops. However, attempting to manually scrub the sediment is risky and could cause further damage, so given the sound is driving you mad, it is best to have a professional handle it.",
